name="twitter:image" content="https://paystage.xyz/og.png"/><script src="/_next/static/chunks/polyfills-42372ed130431b0a.js" noModule=""></script></head><body><div hidden=""><!--$--><!--/$--></div><script>try{var t=localStorage.getItem("paystage.theme");if(t==="light"||t==="dark"){document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme",t)}}catch(e){}</script><header class="site-header" data-scrolled="false"><div class="site-header-inner"><a class="site-brand" aria-label="PayStage" href="/"><svg class="site-brand-mark" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true"><rect width="32" height="32" rx="7" fill="#0a0b0e"></rect><path d="M11 8h6.2c3.1 0 5.3 2 5.3 5s-2.2 5-5.3 5H14v6h-3V8zm3 2.6v4.8h3c1.5 0 2.4-.9 2.4-2.4s-.9-2.4-2.4-2.4h-3z" fill="#6ee7b7"></path><circle cx="23.5" cy="23.5" r="2.5" fill="#34d399"></circle></svg><span>PayStage</span></a><nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Primary"><a href="/#how">How it works</a><a href="/#why">Why now</a><a href="/#agents">For agents</a><a href="/lists">Lists</a><a href="/glossary">Glossary</a><a href="/console">Console</a></nav><div class="site-actions"><button type="button" class="site-icon-button" aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="More">⋯</button><div class="site-wallet"><button type="button" class="site-connect">Connect wallet</button></div></div></div></header><main class="lp-wrap lp-prose"><h1>Privacy</h1><p class="lp-lead">PayStage is a payment-safety tool used by agents. Nothing here requires an account: every tool, the free tier, the paid path and every receipt work signed out. There are no tracking cookies and no pixels. One first-party session cookie can remember the listing token (<code>?from=</code>) you arrived from; it holds only that token and no identifier. Signing in is optional and exists for one reason — to remember your theme and language on another device. This page states exactly what a call records and exactly what an account would store.</p><h2>What a call records</h2><p>One row per call, in our own database:</p><ul><li><strong>when</strong> — a timestamp</li><li><strong>source</strong> — <code>real</code>, <code>synthetic</code> or <code>test</code>, as the caller labels it (unlabelled is recorded as <code>real</code>)</li><li><strong>tool</strong> — which of the tools was called</li><li><strong>client package</strong> and <strong>client version</strong> — the SDK build that made the call, taken from an <code>x-paystage-client</code> header or the user agent when it names one of our packages. This is the build, not you: no IP address, no user-agent string, and nothing that identifies a person is stored. It exists so a release can be checked against what is actually installed.</li><li><strong>channel</strong> — the listing token from <code>?from=</code> on a listing URL, lowercased and limited to <code>[a-z0-9._-]</code> and 32 characters. Nothing else about the visit is read: no IP address, no referrer URL and no user-agent string. A missing or invalid token is stored as null (unknown), never as &quot;direct&quot;.</li><li><strong>decision</strong> and <strong>reason codes</strong> — for example <code>do_not_pay</code> with<!-- --> <code>known drainer</code></li><li><strong>network</strong> — the CAIP-2 id, e.g. <code>eip155:8453</code></li><li><strong>latency</strong> — how long the evaluation took, in milliseconds</li><li><strong>amount</strong> and <strong>payee</strong> — the payment being judged, when one was supplied</li><li><strong>transaction hash</strong> and <strong>payer address</strong> — only when a settlement happened, read from the payment receipt</li><li><strong>request id</strong>, <strong>facilitator status</strong>, <strong>error class</strong> — for debugging a failure</li></ul><h2>What it does not record</h2><ul><li><strong>No IP address, and the free-tier counter is approximate on purpose.</strong> The daily allowance is counted per IP <em>inside one Worker isolate</em>, in that isolate&#x27;s memory, and is never written to the database. A shared counter would have to live somewhere, and every option turned an address into a stored record; so the allowance is deliberately per isolate and therefore approximate at the edges — a caller who spreads across isolates may get a little more than the allowance, which we accept rather than keep a log that identifies people.</li><li><strong>No email address, name or password.</strong> Account creation is optional and uses a wallet signature, so there is nothing to leak and nothing to reset.</li><li><strong>No cookies that identify you.</strong> The only cookie is the session one described above: it stores a listing token, not an identifier, and it expires when the browser session does. No device identifier is written to the database.</li><li><strong>No referrer URL.</strong> The page that sent you is never read or logged. A publisher can attribute a visit only by putting <code>?from=&lt;channel&gt;</code> on a URL that points at PayStage.</li><li><strong>No request bodies.</strong> We record the payment being judged, never the content of your request to the seller.</li><li><strong>No private keys.</strong> PayStage never holds one and cannot sign.</li></ul><h2>If you choose to sign in</h2><p>Optional, and only to carry your preferences between devices. The record is a wallet address and two settings:</p><ul><li><strong>wallet address</strong> — the one that signed the message; it is already public on chain</li><li><strong>theme</strong> — <code>system</code>, <code>light</code> or <code>dark</code></li><li><strong>language</strong> — the locale you picked</li><li><strong>updated_at</strong> — when you last changed them</li></ul><p>Nothing else is stored, no session cookie identifies you across the site, and <strong>no feature requires it</strong>— signing out loses nothing except cross-device sync. Agents are never asked to sign in; the MCP server does not read this at all.</p><h2>On-chain data is public</h2><p>When a payment settles, the transaction — including the payer address, the payee and the amount — is public on Base and can never be removed by us or anyone else. Our row simply echoes what the chain already shows.</p><h2>Who else sees it</h2><ul><li>Cloudflare — hosts the API and the site</li><li>Supabase — our database</li><li>Coinbase (CDP) — the x402 facilitator that verifies and settles paid calls</li></ul><p>None of them receives anything beyond what is listed above.</p><h2>Removing a row</h2><p>Open an issue at<!-- --> <a href="https://github.com/base-buzz/paystage/issues" rel="noopener">github.com/base-buzz/paystage/issues</a> <!-- -->with the transaction hash or request id and we will delete the row. We cannot delete the on-chain transaction, because nobody can.</p><h2>Verifying this page</h2><p>The claim that matters is the field list above. It is checked against the code by<!-- --> <code>scripts/check-privacy.mjs</code> in the repository, so a field added to telemetry without a line here fails CI rather than quietly becoming true.</p><p class="lp-prose-back"><a href="/">← back to PayStage</a> · <a href="/limits">limits</a> ·<!-- --> <a href="https://github.com/base-buzz/paystage/blob/main/LIMITS.md">LIMITS.md</a></p></main><!--$--><!--/$--><script src="/_next/static/chunks/webpack-b54e87df12a9ffcf.js" id="_R_" async=""></script><script>(self.__next_f=self.__next_f||[]).push([0])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1:\"$Sreact.fragment\"\n2:I[77599,[\"2619\",\"static/chunks/2619-04bc32f026a0d946.js\",\"7177\",\"static/chunks/app/layout-1e5f3749e43b61ab.js\"],\"SiteHeader\"]\n3:I[9766,[],\"\"]\n4:I[98924,[],\"\"]\n1e:I[57150,[],\"\"]\n:HL[\"/_next/static/css/90d6d2c4bbe09d17.css\",\"style\"]\n:HL[\"/_next/static/css/1e304f7af79a342b.css\",\"style\"]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"0:{\"P\":null,\"b\":\"FbzxDZZZ_3I6mUwdDp2Hm\",\"p\":\"\",\"c\":[\"\",\"privacy\"],\"i\":false,\"f\":[[[\"\",{\"children\":[\"privacy\",{\"children\":[\"__PAGE__\",{}]}]},\"$undefined\",\"$undefined\",true],